To create a React component that includes a form for users to fill out their personal information and sends the form data to an Express API, you can follow the code example below. This example uses modern JavaScript practices such as `fetch` and `async/await`, along with state management and controlled components.

First, make sure you have the necessary dependencies installed. You will need `react` and `react-dom` for your React component, and `express` for your backend API.

**React Component:**

```jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';

const PersonalInfoForm = () => {
  const [formData, setFormData] = useState({
    name: '',
    birthday: '',
    email: '',
    phone: ''
  });
  const [message, setMessage] = useState('');

  const handleChange = (e) => {
    const { name, value } = e.target;
    setFormData({ ...formData, [name]: value });
  };

  const handleSubmit = async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    try {
      const response = await fetch('http://localhost:3001/submit-form', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Content-Type': 'application/json'
        },
        body: JSON.stringify(formData)
      });
      const data = await response.json();
      setMessage(data.message);
    } catch (error) {
      setMessage('An error occurred while submitting the form.');
    }
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Personal Information Form</h1>
      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
        <div>
          <label>Name:</label>
          <input type="text" name="name" value={formData.name} onChange={handleChange} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label>Birthday:</label>
          <input type="date" name="birthday" value={formData.birthday} onChange={handleChange} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label>Email:</label>
          <input type="email" name="email" value={formData.email} onChange={handleChange} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label>Phone Number:</label>
          <input type="tel" name="phone" value={formData.phone} onChange={handleChange} />
        </div>
        <button type="submit">Submit</button>
      </form>
      {message && <p>{message}</p>}
    </div>
  );
};

export default PersonalInfoForm;
```

**Express API:**

Create a simple Express server that handles the form submission.

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const port = 3001;

app.use(express.json());

app.post('/submit-form', (req, res) => {
  const { name, birthday, email, phone } = req.body;
  // You can add your logic here to handle the form data.
  // For example, you might save it to a database or send an email.
  console.log('Received form data:', req.body);
  res.json({ message: 'Form submitted successfully!' });
});

app.listen(port, () => {
  console.log(`Server listening at http://localhost:${port}`);
});
```

To run this example, follow these steps:

1. Create a React project using `create-react-app`.
2. Replace the contents of `App.js` with the `PersonalInfoForm` component code.
3. Create a new file called `server.js` and paste the Express API code into it.
4. Run the React development server with `npm start` and the Express server with `node server.js`.

Now you have a React component that includes a form for users to fill out their personal information and an Express API that receives and processes the form data.

